<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Jan consumer prices up 13.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Jan consumer prices up 13.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's consumer price index increased 13.4 percent in January year-on-year compared with 11.41 percent in December and 8.93 percent in January 1996, the Federal Bureau of Statistics said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The index, using 1990/91 as base year, rose 2.17 percent in January to 192.11 from 188.03 in December 1996. The index stood at 169.41 in January 1996.</p>
<p>					   Jan	 Dec	   Dec 1995</p>
<p>CONSUMER PRICE  base 1990/91   192.11    188.03	   169.41</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		  +2.17     +1.39	    +0.37</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   +13.40    +11.41	    +8.93</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
